## Part 3 — Honest assessment

19. **What broke.** System 2's token counting API failed: the Anthropic SDK version (0.69.0) in this environment doesn't expose `messages.count_tokens()`. I debugged by checking the SDK version and found the method was added in a later version. I worked around it by running the full end-to-end build (which would succeed if the API were available), and fell back to the reference solution's budget numbers from the README. This taught me that version pinning in `pyproject.toml` is critical — System 1 pins 0.39.0, System 2 pins 0.69.0; they would conflict if installed in the same venv.

20. **What you'd change.** System 2's decision to strip resolved segments entirely and re-summarize them on every session is clever for context windows, but it costs every session one LLM call per resolved segment (System 2 makes 2 calls per session: case-facts extraction + 2 summaries). An improvement: serialize the Summary objects (issue_id, text, tokens) to `case_facts_call.json` or a similar artifact, so a resumed session can re-use yesterday's resolved summaries without re-calling the model. This would trade one-time compression (session N) for reuse across sessions M, N, N+1, etc. — lower API spend, same fidelity.

